{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>You shall not round.</b> He commanded that we not profane ourselves by rounding the head like the practice of fools and drunkards or idolatrous priests, nor by shaving the beard, as they said: הֲדָרַת פָּנִים זָקָן (Shabbat 152b), nor by laceration for the dead, as those who greatly aggrandize human death and mourn excessively over it. And likewise by tattooing a mark to set a sign upon our flesh besides the sign of the covenant."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:58.280081419Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}